---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import QuestionLab from '../../labs/question/QuestionLab.astro';
import { execution, question, choice, captures } from '../../labs/question/model';
---
<BaseLayout title="Question Lab | One answer, the task continues | David Blumenau" description="Watch a real native question pause Claude Engine, receive the recorded Quick setup answer, then continue the same invocation. Isolated Simulator build, local API shim and unreleased Claude-only correction.">
  <main id="main" class="ql-page">
    <section class="ql-hero wrap" id="top"><a class="ql-back" href="/work/connected-agents/"><Icon name="arrow-left" /> The connected agents story</a><div class="ql-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Question Lab / Human direction, mid-task</p><h1>One answer.<br /><em>The task continues.</em></h1></div><p>Sometimes the useful next step is a choice only the person can make. A question in native chat can pause the work, receive that direction and let the same task carry on.</p></div></section>
    <div class="wrap"><QuestionLab /></div>
    <section class="ql-captures wrap" aria-labelledby="ql-captures-title"><header><div><p class="eyebrow">Authentic native pixels</p><h2 id="ql-captures-title">The question.<br /><em>The consequence.</em></h2></div><p>Details from the original device screenshots, paired with the recorded story. Each link opens the full-size capture.</p></header><div class="ql-capture-grid">{captures.map(capture => <figure><a class:list={['ql-capture-window', `ql-focus-${capture.focus}`]} href={`/media/question/${capture.name}.png`} target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label={`Open full-size capture: ${capture.label}`}><img src={`/media/question/${capture.name}.png`} width="1206" height="2622" alt={capture.alt} loading="lazy" /></a><figcaption><strong>{capture.label}</strong><p>{capture.copy}</p><p class="ql-capture-scope">Isolated Simulator; automated participant; local API shim; unreleased Claude-only correction.</p><a href={`/media/question/${capture.name}.png`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Full-size original <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a></figcaption></figure>)}</div><p class="ql-small-note">The previews crop the original screenshots for readability. They do not recreate the native screen. The final text is a drafted plan; none of its actions ran.</p></section>
    <section class="ql-evidence wrap" aria-labelledby="ql-evidence-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">Follow the causal receipt</p><h2 id="ql-evidence-title">An answer received.<br /><em>A turn resumed.</em></h2><p>The original request stayed open. The native answer resolved its pending question, and the actual tool result confirmed the choice before the final text followed.</p><a class="text-link" href="/media/question/receipt.json">Inspect the public receipt <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a></div><div class="ql-evidence-proof"><p class="eyebrow">Actual built-in tool result</p><blockquote>{execution.tool_result.content}</blockquote><p class="ql-small-note">The question, native answer, pending future, tool result and final completion were checked against matching private identities. The public receipt omits those opaque IDs.</p><details class="ql-wire"><summary>See the actual answer map <Icon name="plus" /></summary><p>The visible card’s selection is under the UI header <code>Priority</code>. The native request sent the answer under the <strong>full question text</strong>, as the built-in Claude tool requires.</p><pre><code>{JSON.stringify(execution.native_answer_payload, null, 2)}</code></pre><p>This is the captured native payload with its opaque request ID removed, verified against the private request. The shim forwarded it unchanged.</p></details></div></section>
    <details class="ql-method wrap"><summary>What ran, what was corrected, and what this does not prove <Icon name="plus" /></summary><div class="ql-method-grid"><div><h3>The actual path</h3><p>The existing SwiftUI chat card, controller, SSE decoder and response API ran in a separate iPhone 17 Pro Simulator build. A minimal local API shim forwarded original SSE and the native answer to the original Claude Engine handlers. The model used its real built-in question tool through subscription inference.</p><p>The final native run passed its exact answer-map regression and actual UI flow: two tests, no failures. The successful run made one question tool call, then produced 25 text events after the answer and a 232-character final plan.</p><details><summary>Read the film’s text alternative</summary><p>The fictional task asks for a workshop check-in plan after choosing between Quick setup and More customization. Claude asks: “{question.question}” The automated participant selects {choice} and sends it. The actual tool confirms that answer. The same invocation resumes and visibly produces Chosen direction: Quick setup, followed by a short invite, a shared document and a 20-minute session. Those are drafted suggestions; no invite, document or session was created.</p></details></div><div><h3>A correction in this isolated build</h3><p>The first actual run returned HTTP “answered,” but the built-in tool said the questions were unanswered. The native card had keyed its map by the short UI header. An expected failing regression exposed that mismatch; the isolated Claude path was corrected to use full question text.</p><p>This correction is unreleased. The capture uses an isolated Simulator and local API shim; it does not validate deployed Laravel persistence, production routing or the unmodified released native app. Codex, spoken answers, macOS cards, multi-select and reconnect behavior were not tested here.</p><dl><dt>Engine source</dt><dd><code>{execution.source_revisions['claude-engine']}</code></dd><dt>Native base source</dt><dd><code>{execution.source_revisions['claude-engine-app']}</code></dd><dt>Participant</dt><dd>Automated XCUITest</dd><dt>Native patch</dt><dd>Unreleased; Claude only</dd></dl></div></div></details>
    <section class="ql-distinction wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">Different ways a person can intervene</p><h2>A question about<br /><em>the work itself.</em></h2></div><div><p>This is Claude’s built-in <code>AskUserQuestion</code>: a task needs an answer, and its original question call waits for one.</p><dl><dt>Permission</dt><dd>Decides whether a tool may run.</dd><dt>Attention</dt><dd>A separate notification and durable card flow.</dd><dt>Steering</dt><dd>Adds new guidance to a running task.</dd></dl><a class="text-link" href="/work/connected-agents/">Read the connected agents story <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
